SparkFS
=======

David Pilling's SparkFS, from RISC OS Open's sources
(FileSys/ImageFS/SparkFS), built for this box: archives open as
directories.  SparkFS, its codecs and this application are in the ROM:
!SparkFS is in the Apps icon's directory, and archives are typed and
open with a double-click from the desktop's start.

Double-click !SparkFS, or an archive: SparkFS's icon appears on the
icon bar, and from then on the Filer shows archives as directories --
open them, copy files out of them, and for the archives SparkFS writes,
copy files and directories into them, make directories in them, open and
save the files in them.

The icon bar icon's menu:

  Info         the program's name, author and version
  New archive  a save box for a new, empty archive: Spark file, Spark
               dir, PK arc, Tar or Zip -- drag its icon to a directory
               viewer (or type a full path and press Return); it opens
  Archive      the archives open now
  Choices...   memory, UUcode, the codecs loaded, the archive type and
               compression method new archives get, the scrap directory
  Quit         Filer (the application) or FS too (SparkFS as well)

Drop a file on the icon to encode it: a save box offers Compress, GZip,
UUcode, BtoA, Mime, Boo and DeBoo.  Drop a compressed or encoded file
(compress, gzip, uuencode, BtoA, BinHex) on it to decode it, where it is.

The archives, by file type:

  Archive  &DDC  Spark, PK arc (written too); ArcFS, LHA (.lzh, .lha),
                 ARJ, Zoo, StuffIt, PackIt, Compact Pro (read only)
  Zip      &A91  written too
  Tar      &C46  written too
  PackdDir &68E  read only
  Cabinet  &ABF  read only
  CPIO     &ABA  read only

*SparkFSCreate <type> <name> makes a new archive: 1 Spark, 3 PK arc,
4 Zip, 7 Tar.  *SparkFSMethod <type> <method> sets how files copied into
it are compressed.  *McStuffitMode <mode> chooses what a Mac archive's
files give: 1 the resource fork, 2 the data fork, 3 both (MacBinary, the
default), 4 the longer.

Licences: CDDL 1.0 and Apache 2.0, file by file, and the Info-ZIP
licence for the Zip codec's compression code: the Licences directory
